<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Perfect Squares with Coefficients Other than 1</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02387</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Perfect Squares with Coefficients Other than 1</md:title>
    <md:uuid>a53f8feb-cd8f-4b62-a080-cf735e971752</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001"><title>Warm Up</title>
      
        <exercise id="exer-00001">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00001">Elena says, "<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> can be expanded into <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. Likewise, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> can be expanded into <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>."</para>
            <para id="para-00002">Find an error in Elena's statement and correct the error. Show your reasoning.</para>
            <para id="para-00003"/>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00004">Compare your answer: </para>
            <para id="para-00005"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> is not equivalent to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00006">Applying the <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00001">distributive property</term> to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> gives <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, which is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      
    </section>
  </content>
</document>